{"name":"Cameo White","hex":"#eed8ba","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"cameo","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A piece of jewelry, etc., carved in relief.","A single very brief appearance, especially by a prominent celebrity in a movie or song."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To appear in a cameo role."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cameo"},{"term":"white","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Bright and colourless; reflecting equal quantities of all frequencies of visible light.","Of or relating to Europeans or those of European descent, regardless if their skin has cool or warm undertones."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The color of snow or milk; the color of light containing equal amounts of all visible wavelengths.","A person of European descent with light-colored skin."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/white"}],"entries":[{"title":"Cameo (carving)","blocks":[{"text":"Cameo is a method of carving an object such as an engraved gem, item of jewellery or vessel. It nearly always features a raised (positive) relief image; contrast with intaglio, which has a negative image. Originally, and still in discussing historical work, cameo only referred to works where the relief image was of a contrasting colour to the background; this was achieved by carefully carving a piece of material with a flat plane where two contrasting colours met, removing all the first colour except for the image to leave a contrasting background."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/87/Great_Cameo_of_France_CdM_Paris_Bab264_n1.jpg/330px-Great_Cameo_of_France_CdM_Paris_Bab264_n1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cameo_(carving)","wikidata":"Q28512"},{"title":"White","blocks":[{"text":"White is the lightest color and is achromatic. It is the color of objects such as snow, chalk, and milk, and is the opposite of black. White objects fully reflect and scatter all the visible wavelengths of light. White on television and computer screens is created by a mixture of red, blue, and green light. The color white can be given with white pigments, especially titanium dioxide."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e2/Delphinapterus_leucas_2.jpg/330px-Delphinapterus_leucas_2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/White","wikidata":"Q23444"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f7/Adlerkameo_KHM.jpg/500px-Adlerkameo_KHM.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f7/Adlerkameo_KHM.jpg/1280px-Adlerkameo_KHM.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f7/Adlerkameo_KHM.jpg/500px-Adlerkameo_KHM.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Eagle Cameo, Roman 27 B.C. Two-layered onyx.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AAdlerkameo_KHM.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/68/Cameo_August_BM_Gem3577.jpg/500px-Cameo_August_BM_Gem3577.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/68/Cameo_August_BM_Gem3577.jpg/1280px-Cameo_August_BM_Gem3577.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/68/Cameo_August_BM_Gem3577.jpg/500px-Cameo_August_BM_Gem3577.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Cameo of Roman Emperor Augustus wearing a gorgoneion and a sword-belt. Three-layered sardonyx cameo, Roman artwork, c. 14–20 AD.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ACameo_August_BM_Gem3